After a throwing `act`, the update is queued to the abandoned act queue and never renders. The warning shows that React still sees an active act queue outside `act`. Keeping `IS_REACT_ACT_ENVIRONMENT` set to `true` gives the same result.

Both error paths call `popActScope(prevActQueue, prevActScopeDepth)` ([sync](<url>), [async](<url>)), but [`popActScope`](<url>) only restores `actScopeDepth` and ignores `prevActQueue`. On the success paths, the outermost `act` sets `ReactSharedInternals.actQueue = null` after flushing, which the error paths never do.

