## Steps To Reproduce

1. Attach an `onTransitionRun`, `onTransitionStart`, or `onTransitionCancel` handler to any DOM element.
2. Inspect `e.propertyName`, `e.elapsedTime`, or `e.pseudoElement` on the event object.
3. Observe that these properties are all `undefined`.

### Reproduction Example

```jsx
function App() {
  return (
  <div
  onTransitionRun={e => {
  // Expected: "opacity" (or transitioning property name)
  // Actual: undefined
  console.log('transitionrun propertyName:', e.propertyName);
  console.log('transitionrun elapsedTime:', e.elapsedTime);
  console.log('transitionrun pseudoElement:', e.pseudoElement);
  }}
  onTransitionEnd={e => {
  // Works as expected: "opacity"
  console.log('transitionend propertyName:', e.propertyName);
  }}
  >
  Transition Box
  </div>
  );
}
```

## The current behavior

When `onTransitionRun`, `onTransitionStart`, or `onTransitionCancel` fires, the event object passed to the handler is a base generic `SyntheticEvent` instead of `SyntheticTransitionEvent`. 

Because base `SyntheticEvent` does not implement `TransitionEventInterface`, standard transition properties (`propertyName`, `elapsedTime`, `pseudoElement`) are not normalized and evaluate to `undefined`.

In contrast, `onTransitionEnd` (as well as all four `onAnimation*` events) properly instantiates its corresponding synthetic event constructor.

## The expected behavior

`onTransitionRun`, `onTransitionStart`, and `onTransitionCancel` should receive an instance of `SyntheticTransitionEvent` with normalized properties (`propertyName`, `elapsedTime`, `pseudoElement`), consistent with `onTransitionEnd` and the CSS Transitions specification.

## Root Cause & Fix

In [`packages/react-dom-bindings/src/events/plugins/SimpleEventPlugin.js`](file:///d:/Projects/react/packages/react-dom-bindings/src/events/plugins/SimpleEventPlugin.js), `TRANSITION_CANCEL`, `TRANSITION_RUN`, and `TRANSITION_START` are registered as simple events in `DOMEventProperties.js`, but they were omitted from the switch statement in `SimpleEventPlugin.js`:

```javascript
  case ANIMATION_CANCEL:
  case ANIMATION_END:
  case ANIMATION_ITERATION:
  case ANIMATION_START:
  SyntheticEventCtor = SyntheticAnimationEvent;
  break;
  case TRANSITION_END: // Missing TRANSITION_CANCEL, TRANSITION_RUN, TRANSITION_START
  SyntheticEventCtor = SyntheticTransitionEvent;
  break;
```

Adding `TRANSITION_CANCEL`, `TRANSITION_RUN`, and `TRANSITION_START` to this case resolves the issue. I have a tested fix ready to open as a PR.

