TS emits a plain call expression when `enableForest` is on (`CodegenReactiveFunction.ts`, `CallExpression` case). That branch bypasses `createCallExpression`, which is what wraps hook calls in a `$dispatcherGuard` IIFE. The Rust port calls `maybe_wrap_hook_call` unconditionally, so `@enableForest @enableEmitHookGuards` produced an extra guard IIFE around `useState()` that TS does not emit.

