### The generated code for `f` (`-C opt-level=2`, nightly)

```asm
f:
  movq  (%rsi), %rax
  lock incq (%rax)
  jle  .LBB4_12
  ...
  movq  32(%rsi), %r11  ; s[4] loaded into r11
  lock incq (%r11)
  jle  .LBB4_8
  movq  %rsp, %r11  ; shrink-wrapped prologue: the probe bound overwrites r11
  subq  $36864, %r11
.LBB4_6:
  subq  $4096, %rsp
  movq  $0, (%rsp)
  cmpq  %r11, %rsp
  jne  .LBB4_6
  subq  $72, %rsp
  ...
  movq  %r11, 40(%rsp)  ; the clobbered r11 is stored as r[4]
  ...
  callq  keep
```

The prologue is placed after the five increments because their failure paths do not return (`loop {}`), so they do not need a frame. The placement apparently checks that EFLAGS is not live at the insertion point, but not that `r11`, the scratch register of the inline probe, is not.

