Incremental lockfile-only installation can retain a peer-bound npm package while removing one of its required ordinary dependency mappings during version deduplication. This report concerns the generated snapshot's completeness, **not a demonstrated runtime execution failure**.

## Independent public-package reproduction

This fixture was created independently from three public npm packages. No application manifest, application lockfile, application source, private registry, or synthetic package/import is used. Both locks below were generated by Deno, never hand-edited.

Save as `package.before.json`:

```json
