## Summary

`mock.reset()` in Deno's `node:test` polyfill only cleared call history. Node's `MockTracker.reset()` also restores methods mocked with `mock.method()` back to their originals.

This mirrors the existing `MockModuleContext.resetCalls()` approach: when `mock.reset()` iterates `activeMocks` and calls `resetCalls()`, method mocks (those with a restore hook) restore the original property descriptor. Standalone `mock.fn()` still only clears call history (`restore` is `undefined`), matching the existing Deno fixture.

Fixes #36881

## Repro (Node vs Deno)

```js
import assert from "node:assert/strict";
import { mock } from "node:test";

const foo = { bar: () => "original" };
mock.method(foo, "bar", () => "mocked");
assert.equal(foo.bar(), "mocked");
mock.reset();
assert.equal(foo.bar(), "original"); // Node: pass; Deno before: fail
```

